    description: "Split out of WI-rutup 2026-10-26. python.yaml rows asyncio.start_unix_server (and loop.create_unix_server) under net_listen, and go net.ListenUnix (go.yaml ~:376, kept to the C connect() precedent by WI-potog), name a Unix-socket LISTENER: under ADR-0050 section 1's medium axiom the medium is local IPC, not the network, but the vocabulary has no ipc-side deferred-crossing value -- net_listen is the only listen boundary (deferred_crossing axis: net_listen, db_compose). A row edit cannot fix it; it needs a vocabulary ruling: (a) add an ipc_listen deferred-crossing value (registry + ADR-0050 section 2 table + catalogue rows + the disclosure clauses net_listen carries), or (b) rule that net_listen names \"a listener\" regardless of medium and say so in its definition. Owner decision; nothing to implement until then."  # acf1
